WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.861
Twenty nine parts, each cut at a different speed, each

2
00:00:03.961 --> 00:00:08.924
with its surface roughness measured. Faster cutting, rougher surface.

3
00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:12.733
Which straight line describes them? Start with the

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:16.092
laziest one: flat, at the average roughness.

5
00:00:16.183 --> 00:00:20.003
Every part misses the line by some amount. Square

6
00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:22.803
each miss, and draw it as a square.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.295
Add up their areas. That sum is the score,

8
00:00:26.395 --> 00:00:29.208
and a smaller sum is a better line.

9
00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:32.351
Now tilt the line about the centre of the

10
00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:35.792
cloud. The squares shrink, and the sum falls.

11
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.272
Keep tilting, past the cloud, and the squares

12
00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.896
grow again. The sum comes back up.

13
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.077
Every slope has a score, and the scores

14
00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:48.500
make a parabola. It has exactly one floor.

15
00:00:48.616 --> 00:00:51.684
Bring the line back down to the floor.

16
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.845
Nobody needs to slide anything. Set the slope of the

17
00:00:55.945 --> 00:00:59.752
parabola to zero and the floor has a closed form:

18
00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:03.340
the cross products over the squares of speed.

19
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:09.470
Here that is 0.01315 microns per metre a minute.

20
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:14.862
Look closely at the floor. The formula's slope sits at the minimum, not

21
00:01:14.962 --> 00:01:19.635
near it. Any other line is worse, by an amount you can compute.

22
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.196
That is what least squares means. It is a claim

23
00:01:23.296 --> 00:01:26.970
about this parabola, and you just watched it hold.

24
00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:30.864
The flat line from the start was not wasted. Its

25
00:01:30.964 --> 00:01:35.311
squares are the total variation, nine point zero three.

26
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.055
The floor's squares are what the line

27
00:01:38.155 --> 00:01:41.108
leaves unexplained, nought point two six.

28
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.296
One minus their ratio is R squared: the share of the

29
00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:50.220
total variation the line accounts for, ninety seven per cent.

30
00:01:50.316 --> 00:01:55.126
Regression, ANOVA, and the gauge study that comes next all

31
00:01:55.226 --> 00:01:59.528
split this same total. The line is found, not drawn.

